  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Untreated AISI 316L has a naturally formed, non-optimized surface oxide layer.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A controlled oxidation treatment will produce a Cr2O3-rich passivation film on AISI 316L.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The resulting Cr2O3-rich film will be uniform and dense.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6908586::web::001::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Cr2O3-rich film will be coherent.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Cr2O3-rich film will be self-healing.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6908586::web::001::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "A Cr2O3-rich passivation film is the primary mechanism governing the enhanced corrosion resistance of treated AISI 316L under reactor conditions.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6908586::web::001::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The density, uniformity, and stability of the Cr2O3-rich film make it an effective barrier between the environment and the steel substrate.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6908586::web::001::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Cr2O3-rich film hinders diffusion of dissolved oxygen and other aggressive ions to the underlying steel.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6908586::web::001::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Restricted transport through the film reduces anodic dissolution of the steel.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6908586::web::001::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Cr2O3-rich film delays pitting initiation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Oxidation-treated specimens will have significantly lower corrosion current densities than untreated specimens.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Oxidation-treated specimens will have higher EIS impedance than untreated specimens.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Oxidation-treated specimens will initiate pitting later than untreated specimens.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "High-temperature water at approximately 300°C under controlled electrochemical potentials simulates reactor coolant conditions relevant to the hypothesis.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A rapid increase in current indicates breakdown of the protective film.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed mechanism should hold near 300°C within stable electrochemical-potential limits typical of nuclear-reactor operation.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Extreme water-chemistry variations and transient conditions may lie outside the valid domain of the mechanism.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The long-term stability and self-healing capacity of the film under dynamic reactor chemistry and irradiation are uncertain.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
